=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ BISON @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt GNU Bison @VERSION@ for OpenVMS
1 'NOTICE
=prompt GNU Bison is free software under the GNU General Public License v3 or later.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [BISON.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for GNU Bison
    At system startup: to define BISON$ROOT at every boot, add this line to
    SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after the line for M4$STARTUP.COM):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:BISON$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the bison command, add this line to LOGIN.COM:
    $ @BISON$ROOT:[000000]BISON$SETUP.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE BISON removes the product and deassigns BISON$ROOT.
